static const char HELP[] =
    "usage: pow [-h] [--log FILE] [--log-raw FILE] [--log-mb MB] [--replay FILE]\n"
    "           [--follow FILE] [--sudo] [--no-sudo] [--interval MS] [--no-media]\n"
    "           [--no-smc] [--smc-all] [--no-temps] [--charts {auto,pixels,text}]\n"
    "           [--ane-max W] [--headless]\n"
    "\n"
    "pow: a live view of power, load, temperature and fans on Apple Silicon, like top.\n"
    "\n"
    "By default pow is a display only: it reads, draws, and writes nothing to disk. With --log it also records, like\n"
    "sar. It starts without sudo: load, GPU and SoC power, SMC power, fans, temperatures and power mode need none. The\n"
    "private data, CPU and ANE watts, needs `sudo powermetrics`: press P and pow asks for your password and switches,\n"
    "without restarting (or start that way with --sudo).\n"
    "\n"
    "What it shows\n"
    "  header        time, power mode (High Power, Automatic, Low Power) and source (charger, or battery %), total\n"
    "                watts (now, 60 s average, peak), whole-machine watts, the hottest temperature, fan rpm\n"
    "  units         ANE, GPU, CPU watts (now, 60 s average, peak) and load %; ANE load is an estimate from its power\n"
    "  charts        CPU, GPU, ANE and TEMP over time, newest at the right; TEMP only when there is room, and a\n"
    "                thin rule between the charts when there is room for that. CPU and GPU show load (0-100%); ANE\n"
    "                shows watts, scaled to the 95th percentile of what's on screen (a sample above it is white).\n"
    "                E lays CPU and GPU watts over their load as a white line. Three y labels at the right; the\n"
    "                name and current reading by the origin\n"
    "  Space         cycles the charts: bars; one stacked area of load (E and P cores, GPU, ANE estimated, each\n"
    "                unit a third of the height) with the hottest temperature as a quiet line; and bars whose\n"
    "                dots are green, yellow above 70% and red above 90% (TEMP: 70 and 85 C; ANE: of its\n"
    "                estimated full power) over dark dots in the unit's color\n"
    "  big view      at 160x48 or more: ENC/DEC, temperatures by group (P-cores, E-cores, GPU, die, SSD, battery) and a\n"
    "                chart of the hottest one; at the right, SMC power, fans, every core with its watts (codenames\n"
    "                for M1 and M2), and SoC power. Below 160x48 the compact view fits 80x24 and grows to fill more.\n"
    "                \"?\" in a row's description is a guess at what an undocumented channel measures\n"
    "\n"
    "Charts and gauges\n"
    "  In a terminal that speaks the Kitty graphics protocol (Ghostty, Kitty, WezTerm) they are LED dot-matrix\n"
    "  images; pow asks the terminal at startup. Anywhere else (Terminal.app, tmux, ssh) they are text: block\n"
    "  characters and thin lines. --charts overrides the check.\n"
    "\n"
    "Recording and playback\n"
    "  pow --log FILE         also write each sample as a CSV row in FILE: UTC time, CPU/GPU/ANE mW, GPU, cluster and\n"
    "                         per-core active %, and fan rpm. FILE is a ring buffer of two halves: FILE is the newest,\n"
    "                         FILE.1 the older; together at most --log-mb. Its folder must exist. ENC/DEC,\n"
    "                         temperatures, SoC and SMC power are live only and are not saved\n"
    "  pow --log-raw FILE     also keep the raw powermetrics output in FILE, the same way (starts with sudo)\n"
    "  pow --replay FILE      run through a finished --log CSV or raw powermetrics file, then print the last frame\n"
    "  pow --follow FILE      show a --log CSV or raw file that another pow is writing, keeping up as it rotates\n"
    "  pow --headless --log FILE\n"
    "                         record only, for scripts: no screen and no keys; sudo powermetrics into the CSV until\n"
    "                         Ctrl-C, SIGINT or SIGTERM. sudo must already hold your password (run `sudo -v` first)\n"
    "\n"
    "Private data (sudo)\n"
    "  pow                    starts on IOReport, no password. On macOS 27 the CPU and ANE energy counters only update\n"
    "                         while something privileged (powermetrics) samples them, so those watts wait for P;\n"
    "                         residency, GPU watts and the rest work from the start\n"
    "  P                      asks for your password (pow steps out of its screen for the prompt), then runs\n"
    "                         `sudo powermetrics` from there on. Ctrl-C or a wrong password goes back, still without\n"
    "  pow --sudo             start with `sudo powermetrics`, asking first, as pow used to\n"
    "  pow --no-sudo          never ask: no P, and CPU and ANE watts show \"needs sudo\"\n"
    "\n"
    "q quits (so does Ctrl-C). P switches to sudo, once. E shows or hides the power line. Space cycles the charts.\n"
    "\n"
    "options:\n"
    "  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n"
    "\n"
    "recording and playback:\n"
    "  --log FILE            also write each sample as a CSV row in FILE (and\n"
    "                        FILE.1); display only without it\n"
    "  --log-raw FILE        also keep the raw powermetrics output in FILE (and\n"
    "                        FILE.1)\n"
    "  --log-mb MB           most disk each log may use, both halves together\n"
    "                        (default: 64)\n"
    "  --replay FILE         run through a finished log, then print the last frame\n"
    "  --follow FILE         show a log another pow is writing\n"
    "  --headless            record only, for scripts: needs --log and sudo already\n"
    "                        holding your password; no screen, no keys\n"
    "\n"
    "sources:\n"
    "  --sudo                start with sudo powermetrics, asking for your password\n"
    "                        first; without it pow starts on IOReport and P\n"
    "                        switches\n"
    "  --no-sudo             never use sudo: no P; CPU and ANE watts show \"needs\n"
    "                        sudo\"\n"
    "  --interval MS         sample period in ms (default: 1000)\n"
    "  --no-media            skip IOReport: ENC/DEC, per-core watts, SoC power\n"
    "  --no-smc              skip the SMC: whole-machine power, SMC power rows,\n"
    "                        fans, core and GPU temperatures\n"
    "  --smc-all             also list every other SMC power key that moves, by raw\n"
    "                        name\n"
    "  --no-temps            skip temperatures\n"
    "\n"
    "display:\n"
    "  --charts {auto,pixels,text}\n"
    "                        pixels: LED dots by Kitty graphics; text: block\n"
    "                        characters; auto: ask the terminal (default)\n"
    "  --ane-max W           ANE watts that count as 100% load; rises to any higher\n"
    "                        peak seen (default: 7.5)\n";
